 "transcript": [
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "roomba e5 wont charge properly, sometimes it does sometimes it doesnt"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "From what you have described, the most likely cause is the battery or charger. Check the charger is plugged into a working socket and fully into the vacuum (or the robot is seated on its dock), and wipe the charging contacts clean and dry. Was the charger, socket or contacts the problem (and is it sorted), does the charging light never come on, or is the charger fine with the light on?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Light on the base comes on when it docks. The contacts were dull and greasy so I wiped them and it's charged 4 nights in a row now, no error. No heat or smell from it either."
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "Good news, that has sorted it. If it happens again, start with the same check. Is there anything else I can help with?"
  }
 ],
